  "body": "## Symptom\n\nEvery custom model magpie writes into `~/.factory/settings.json` (`customModels`, ids `custom:magpie/*`) is treated by Droid as non-reasoning. Droid's session provenance logs show:\n\n```\n{\"setting\":\"reasoningEffort\",\"value\":\"none\",\"reason\":[\"reasoning_clamped\"]}\n```\n\nThe user's configured reasoning effort is silently clamped to `none` on every model magpie serves, even though the gateway's `/v1/models` advertises reasoning levels for those models (e.g. `devin/swe-2` → `supported_reasoning_levels: [medium,high,max]`; `codex/gpt-6.1-sol` → `[low,medium,high,xhigh,max,ultra]`).\n\n## Root cause\n\n`internal/agent/droid.go` → `droidEntriesAt` emits each `droidEntry` with only `{model, id, displayName, baseUrl, apiKey, provider, maxContextLimit, maxOutputTokens, noImageSupport}`. It never emits `reasoningEffort`.\n\nPer Factory's BYOK docs, `reasoningEffort` on a custom model is the default effort new sessions start at, and setting it is what unlocks the off/low/medium/high picker for that model. A custom model without it (and without a `baseModelId` Droid recognizes) gets `supportedReasoningEfforts: [\"none\"]`, so Droid clamps the session's effort to `none`.\n\nMagpie rewrites its `custom:magpie/*` entries on every sync, so hand-editing `settings.json` doesn't survive — the fix has to live in what magpie writes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `~/.factory/settings.json` `customModels` entries written by magpie have no `reasoningEffort`.\n- `~/.factory/logs/droid-log-*.log` shows `reasoningEffort\":\"none\"` plus `reasoning_clamped` provenance for magpie-served models.\n- Manually adding `\"reasoningEffort\": \"high\"` to a magpie entry makes Droid send the effort — confirmed in magpie's `usage.jsonl`.\n",
